## Intent & Decisions
User wanted a new review skill inspired by the deleted code-review agent team (removed in f62a979), but scoped to code style only, since built-in /code-review handles correctness. Named `cs-review`. Two agents: one meticulously validating Functional Core, Imperative Shell (https://functional-architecture.org/functional_core_imperative_shell/), one validating Locality of Behaviour (https://htmx.org/essays/locality-of-behaviour/) in design and layout.
Decisions made by the agent (not asked): agent names fcis-reviewer and locality-reviewer; no Codex debate, no agent teams, no risk lanes (the old skill's complexity was deliberately not carried over); agents run the diff commands themselves rather than receiving pasted diffs; the lead verifies every finding before reporting; severities must-fix / should-fix / consider; no --fix mode. Minor bump 0.30.1 -> 0.31.0.

## Actions & Verification
