Trial run: built a throwaway Python repo in the session scratchpad with planted violations (clock and env reads in domain logic, injected db, interleaved SMTP send, argument mutation, import-time monkeypatch of orders.total). Ran each agent body through a general-purpose subagent (the plugin agents could not be loaded mid-session). fcis found R4, R1, R2, R5, R8, R9, R7 with a correct effect inventory; locality found L1 (D3 monkeypatch), L3 (D4 env/clock), L9 (process name). Both outputs followed the specified format.
Not verified: invoking /cs-review end to end with the real subagent_type names abatilo-core:fcis-reviewer and abatilo-core:locality-reviewer, which needs a plugin reload.

