## Findings & Constraints
The two principles can conflict (FCIS separates, LoB co-locates). Both agent prompts and the skill resolve it the same way as AGENTS.md: a shell calling a well-named core function with explicit arguments is local and correct. Keep that rule in all three files if editing.
lib/codex.sh copies only gh-stack, git-commit, repo-explore to Codex; cs-review is Claude Code only because it depends on plugin agents. README says so.
Pre-existing uncommitted changes to claude_settings.json and lib/codex.sh were left unstaged; they are the user's.

